1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,720
Welcome to the model flow lab. This edited walkthrough uses captured lab screens and
outputs from real Meta

2
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:15,011
API calls. We follow one tomato through an accelerated video, then connect its visual
history to an

3
00:00:15,011 --> 00:00:18,442
inspection workflow. The product name is still undecided.

4
00:00:18,442 --> 00:00:21,016
No live sensor readings were supplied.

5
00:00:21,667 --> 00:00:26,095
First, Muse Voice Transcribe turns a spoken request into text.

6
00:00:26,095 --> 00:00:32,738
The original tomato video is silent, so this test uses a separately synthesized
demonstration request.

7
00:00:32,738 --> 00:00:37,166
The real model returned the transcript shown in the lab.

8
00:00:37,166 --> 00:00:42,037
That text is included in the history passed to the planner.

9
00:00:42,037 --> 00:00:44,252
Here is the demonstration request.

10
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:48,750
DEMO REQUEST: Check this tomato batch. Compare earlier and later observations.

11
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:55,294
Tell me what to inspect next, and ask for a sensor measurement if evidence is missing.

12
00:00:55,933 --> 00:01:01,074
Next, SAM three point one receives the video and the short prompt, tomato.

13
00:01:01,074 --> 00:01:07,400
It returns an object box and a pixel mask for the tomato in each analyzed frame.

14
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:13,332
We decoded masks for all one hundred and ten frames and rendered this overlay movie.

15
00:01:13,332 --> 00:01:16,100
SAM supplies the object's location and shape.

16
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:20,054
It does not assign an inspection or food safety verdict.

17
00:01:20,667 --> 00:01:25,897
Muse Spark analyzes the full video and returns eight structured checkpoint
observations.

18
00:01:25,897 --> 00:01:32,870
In this run, it described increasing gray textured coverage near the stem, followed by
surface depression

19
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:40,279
and wrinkling. The lab lets you select a checkpoint and read the saved observation
with its visibility

20
00:01:40,279 --> 00:01:46,816
limits. These are visual categories. The accelerated playback does not reveal the real
storage duration.

21
00:01:47,467 --> 00:01:54,649
Rescue is the decision workflow. Application code maps Spark's visual category to the
proposed inspection

22
00:01:54,649 --> 00:02:02,789
priority. Here the displayed points increase from thirty five, to seventy, to one
hundred as visible concern

23
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:07,577
increases. These are heuristic priority points, not probabilities of spoilage.

24
00:02:07,577 --> 00:02:15,238
Because no gas or environmental measurements exist for this video, the sensor channel
and combined score

25
00:02:15,238 --> 00:02:16,196
remain unavailable.

26
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,563
Muse Wonder powers the Investigator planning step.

27
00:02:19,563 --> 00:02:26,669
It made a real history tool call, received the saved video observations and returned
this read only plan.

28
00:02:26,669 --> 00:02:32,196
It compared earlier and later evidence, requested additional views and identified the
missing sensor

29
00:02:32,196 --> 00:02:34,959
protocol. This is a full clip summary.

30
00:02:34,959 --> 00:02:43,249
The model did not perform a physical measurement or an A B group test, and it did not
approve stock for

31
00:02:43,249 --> 00:02:43,644
sale.

32
00:02:44,267 --> 00:02:47,348
ShelfWatch keeps the evidence under one batch identity.

33
00:02:47,348 --> 00:02:51,971
The timeline connects each checkpoint, mask and observation to the same sample.

34
00:02:51,971 --> 00:02:57,750
In the lab you can create a follow up task and mark the demonstration reviewed.

35
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:00,446
Those actions are local to the browser.

36
00:03:00,446 --> 00:03:08,151
In the future app, a vendor would confirm an actual inspection or stock outcome, and
the next plan would use

37
00:03:08,151 --> 00:03:09,306
that saved history.

38
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:15,557
Finally, the model receipts show response identifiers, usage and the planning tool
trace.

39
00:03:15,557 --> 00:03:21,180
This demonstrates all four required model integrations and how their outputs fit
together.

40
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:28,101
The next build step is to connect real batch storage, controlled sensor sessions and
human confirmed

41
00:03:28,101 --> 00:03:35,888
actions. This video is an explanation of the lab, not evidence of food safety or
validated shelf life.
